Z||000005||Dale||09-10-1999||03:16 AM||||Do you have AC? Also check the PCV.  If you hear it at idle, take a piece of garden hose or simmiler and use it like a stethascope,  you can usualy pinpoint noises this way.||||reg||
Z||000006||WisconsinGT||09-10-1999||11:19 AM||||Dale, I do have AC. It has not been working for two weeks now. Guess what? The noise started about two weeks ago as well. ||||reg||
Z||000007||Dale||09-10-1999||01:33 PM||||Hmmmmmmm, I would be willing to bet its the pully on the AC.  They have a clutch system to engage the pully when you turn the AC on.  You might take the belt off and see if the noise goes away (providing that the belt does not power anything else). <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||
